<p>Me gusta. This version is a tick better.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Things&nbsp;I&nbsp;like:</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>-Living organisms only. Avoids tons of plot holes.<br />
-Prom Labs not being a complete screwup. A lot more believeable, a lot less cliche, and leaves me with quite a few questions.<br />
-Added some limits and dimensions, leaving reasonable ambiguity as well.<br />
-I do like the squick, but there appears to be little reason for it, see below.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Things&nbsp;I&nbsp;don't&nbsp;like:</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>-Kirk still seems like the least professional researcher in existence (hyperbole, of course). Even under an interview, one would expect a Foundation researcher to be more formal.<br />
-Containers: how big? Are they my Tupperware containers? Or toxic waste barrels?<br />
-Second paragraph of the description has some redundancy in regards to the stage section.<br />
-The -3's seem to squick for no reason, at least not any aforementioned one. Mention the gun's on the wall before you shoot it, y'know? Why do they weirdly slaughter stuff? Murdering an object to death is enough to defend -1, right?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Things&nbsp;I&nbsp;feel&nbsp;neutral&nbsp;about:</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>-The touchy-feely doesn't really get me. It feels kinda shoehorned in. That being said, it adds another aspect to think about to this article.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>A weird thing to note: You went from effect oriented to squick to touchy-feely all in one fell scip. Huh. Don't try doing to much in one scip, to me this one has less direct impact, but I suppose more overall.</p>
<p>All in all, +1.</p>

