<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Project Planet cell</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Should 'cell' not also be capitalized?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>higher ups</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Feel like a dash would make this look less janky.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Henderson: This sounds like it was top secret.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This observation seems nonsensical. There's lots of Labs projects that could feasibly be considered black operations. Surely they have an understanding of this? 'Top secret' could easily be replaced by 'it must've been exciting,' and the conversation wouldn't miss a beat.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Higher ups</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is the second time you've used 'higher-ups to denote a group of individuals in the apex of command. It feels repetitive. Perhaps you could replace it with 'PR' or something like that? That way, it'd be more clear who the company was denying themselves to.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>corpses. Just, Jesus.The</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Spacing.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I liked this. I think you manage to capture the sense of an experiment going wrong rather well; the pacing is good, the characters are decent enough, in that their motivations make sense and their dialogue is feasible, and the Foundation's response to the situation seems appropriate. Good job all around.</p>

